    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "USE OF PROCEEDS We estimate that our net proceeds from the sale of \u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 common shares in this offering will be approximately $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\nmillion, based on an assumed initial public offering price of $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 per share, which is the midpoint of our estimated offering price range set forth on the cover page of this prospectus, after deducting underwriting\ndiscounts, commissions and estimated expenses payable by us related to the offering. If the underwriters exercise their option in full to purchase \u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 additional common shares, our estimated net proceeds will be\napproximately $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 million, after deducting underwriting discounts, commissions and estimated expenses payable by us related to the offering. Each $1.00 increase or decrease in the assumed initial public offering price of $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 per share, which is the midpoint of our estimated offering\nprice range set forth on the cover page of this pros",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk Factors See \u201cRisk Factors\u201d and the other information included in this prospectus for a discussion of factors you should carefully consider before deciding to invest in our common shares. Proposed Nasdaq trading symbol for the Common Shares \u201cWWB.\u201d 10 Table of Contents The number of common shares to be outstanding after the offering is based on 15,491,686 common shares, including\n1,133,155 restricted shares subject to repurchase rights that lapse, 31,897,927 Series A preferred shares, 5,582,139 Series A junior preferred shares, and 15,948,971 Series B preferred shares outstanding as of June\u00a030, 2026, and excludes: \u220e 1,944,516 common shares issuable upon the exercise of outstanding options under our Amended and Restated 2025 Equity\nIncentive Plan, or the 2025 Plan, as of June\u00a030, 2026, with a weighted-average exercise price of $0.01 per share, as more fully described in the section tit",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If you invest in our common shares during this offering, your ownership interest will be immediately diluted to the extent of the difference between the initial public\noffering price per share of our common shares and the pro forma as adjusted net tangible book value per share of our common shares immediately after the closing of this offering. Our historical net tangible book value as of June\u00a030, 2026 was $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003million, or $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003per share of our common\nshares. Our historical net tangible book value is the amount of our total tangible assets less our total liabilities, excluding the deferred offering costs of $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003million. Historical net tangible book value per share\nrepresents historical net tangible book value divided by the number of common shares outstanding as of June\u00a030, 2026. Our pro forma net tangible book value as\nof June\u00a030, 2026 was $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003million or $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003per share. Pro f",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Principal Shareholders",
      "excerpt": "PRINCIPAL SHAREHOLDERS The following table sets forth information with respect to the beneficial ownership of our common shares as of June\u00a030, 2026, and following the completion of the\noffering for: \u220e each beneficial owner of 5% or more of our outstanding common shares (including common shares issuable upon conversion of\npreferred shares); \u220e each of our directors and executive officers; and \u220e all of our directors and executive officers as a group. We have granted the underwriters an option to purchase \u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 common shares at the initial public offering price of $\u2003\u2003 per common\nshare, which is the midpoint of the price range set forth on the cover page of this prospectus, less underwriting discounts and commissions. Beneficial ownership\nis determined in accordance with the rules of the SEC. These rules generally attribute beneficial ownership of securities to persons who possess sole or shar",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "DIVIDEND POLICY Since our incorporation, we have not declared or paid any dividends on our issued share capital. We expect to continue incurring losses for the\u00a0foreseeable\nfuture\u00a0and therefore do not currently\u00a0anticipate\u00a0paying dividends on our common shares. We cannot predict how any potential future earnings may be\u00a0allocated, as this will depend on the Company\u2019s financial position,\nbusiness\u00a0needs\u00a0and other relevant circumstances at that time.\u00a0As a result, investors in our common shares will benefit in the foreseeable future only if our common shares appreciate in value. Any future determination related to our\ndividend policy will be made at the discretion of our board of directors and will depend upon, among other factors, our results of operations, capital requirements, financial condition, contractual restrictions, business prospects, any future debt\nagreements or applicable laws and",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
